wave: 60
mode: interactive
# Owner's standing cap: concurrency 2 (config max_concurrent is 5). Merges run
# SEQUENTIALLY and never with concurrent full suites.
max_concurrent_override: 2
# 2026-10-22: THREE cards are active against this cap of 2, on the owner's explicit
# "dispatch 264" while wave 53's two cards were still in fix rounds. Recorded as an
# authorised breach rather than left to be inferred from the active list. The cap's
# stated purpose -- merges run sequentially and never with concurrent full suites -- is
# intact: no full-suite run is permitted in any of the three worktrees, each redirects
# its suite lock to a scratch path, and no merge is pending. The cap returns to 2 when
# wave 53 lands.
#
# 2026-10-22, later (run resume, owner's "commit the cards and run the wave"): the
# breach is OVER and the cap is honoured again at 2. Both slots were held by STALLED
# pipelines -- no agent was running for either card in the resuming session -- so the
# run began with `run resume` rather than by starting new cards. CARD-264 escalated at
# the rebase step (7-region semantic conflict with main over _ADAPTER_COUNT; see its
# card), which freed one slot; CARD-270 took it. CARD-262 keeps the other and resumes
# at review cycle 2. Nothing was force-started: 1 resumed + 1 new = 2.
#
# 2026-10-23, owner's "start CARD-264": the card takes the slot that CARD-270's merge
# freed. 1 active against a cap of 2, so the second slot stays deliberately empty --
# this card's build gate IS the full suite (impact_set.py answers FULL on the narrowed
# diff), it holds the board's real lock for the duration, and the cap's stated purpose
# is that a full suite never runs beside a live pipeline. The owed rebase was taken
# first: merge 99782837 brought wave 54's two merged cards in, clean and with ZERO file
# overlap measured (main's 25 changed paths intersect none of this card's six), unlike
# the first rebase which carried a seven-region semantic conflict and was escalated.
# Escalation CLOSED 2026-10-23: owner chose option 1 (fix S-1..S-4, then certify with a
# re-entry cycle 4). Card back to `review` and back in the slot.
# CARD-264 MERGED 066ddc1f 2026-10-23, worktree removed.
# 2026-10-23, owner's "run CARD-271": wave 55 opens with the owner's bugs-first order. 1 active against
# a cap of 2; the second slot stays empty because solver.js/admin.css are this card's for the duration
# and the three cards queued behind it (CARD-267, CARD-269, CARD-268) all touch them.

